{title: 363 - Lord, Whose Love in Humble Service}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Church}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Dm/A]Lord, whose love [Gm]in [Am]humble service
[C/E]Bore the [F]weight of human need,
[F/A]Who upon [Gm]the [Am]cross, forsaken,
[C7/E]Worked Your [F]mercy's perfect deed:
[F/A]We, Your servants, [C/G]bring the [Gm]worship
[Am]Not of [F]voice alone, but heart;
[Gm]Consecrating [F/A]to Your purpose
[F]Every gift [Dm/F]which [C/E]You [Dm]impart.

Verse 2:
[Dm/A]Still Your [C7/Bb]children [Gm]wander [Am]homeless;
[C/E]Still the [F]hungry cry for bread;
[F/A]Still the [C7/Bb]captives [Am]long for [F]freedom;
[C7/E]Still in [F]grief we mourn our dead.
[F/A]As you, Lord, [C/G]in deep compassion
[Am]Healed the [F]sick and freed the soul,
[Gm]By Your Spirit [F/A]send Your power
[F]To our [Dm/F]world [F]to [Dm/F]make [C/E]it [Dm]whole.

Verse 3:
[Dm/A]As we worship, [Am]grant us vision,
[C/E]Till your [F]love's revealing light
[F/A]In its [Dm/A]height [Gm]and [Am]depth and greatness
[C7/E]Dawns upon [F]our quickened sight,
[F/A]Making known [C/G]the needs and [Gm]burdens
[Am]Your compassion [F]bids us bear,
[Gm]Stirring us [F]to ardent service,
[F]Your abundant [Dm/F]life to share.
